text:
jo: Heads-up — ran into a telemetry oddball in the Node sampleapp during onboarding. Incoming x-request-id is present but disappears when work is offloaded to a background tick/worker. Repro and logs below.

meera: that sounds like an AsyncLocalStorage context loss. Which offload pattern? setImmediate, worker_threads, or a queue lib?

dan: seen this when folks use setImmediate or spawn worker_threads without propagating context. Some queue libs also serialize/deserialize and lose headers.

jo: repro (tiny):
```js
// handler.js
const { AsyncLocalStorage } = require('async_hooks');
const als = new AsyncLocalStorage();
app.post('/start', (req, res) => {
  const id = req.headers['x-request-id'] || generateId();
  als.run({ rid: id }, () => {
    // immediate background work
    setImmediate(async () => {
      // our fetch call relies on OTEL hook to inject, but ALS not present here in some runtimes
      await fetch('https://internal/svc', { method: 'POST' });
    });
    res.status(202).send('queued');
  });
});
```

jo: trimmed logs: 
2026-02-01T09:00:00.001Z sampleapp INFO incoming route=/start req_id=req-bg-42
2026-02-01T09:00:00.010Z sampleapp DEBUG background.http.outgoing host=internal x-request-id=-
2026-02-01T09:00:00.050Z sampleapp INFO background job complete req_id=-

olivia: yikes. That dash means header missing, not redacted. In JSON logs prod redaction earlier converted null->"[redacted]" in some dashboards which made this silent.

meera: two things we should do: 1) make our OTEL outgoing hook attempt to re-inject allowlisted headers (x-request-id, traceparent) from AsyncLocalStorage when the outgoing span is created, 2) update the logging redaction plugin to distinguish "missing" vs "masked" so dashboards can show a clear loss vs PII redaction.

dan: also add a small e2e in the sampleapp that covers setImmediate + worker_threads + an in-process queue (bullmq) to catch regressions. And document that if you use external worker processes you must explicitly propagate request-id.

jo: I prototyped a minimal change: middleware seeds ALS, and the otel http hook does: headers['x-request-id'] = headers['x-request-id'] || als.getStore()?.rid; works for the repro. Will open PR.

olivia: remember: do NOT re-inject Authorization. Add an allowlist to the reinjector and tests to ensure we never copy auth headers.

meera: action items: @jo open PR with ALS middleware + e2e; @dan add otel hook reinjection with allowlist; @olivia update redaction plugin docs and JSON masking behavior. I'll file an umbrella issue. :white_check_mark:

telemetry-bot: Created issue #4999: "Node sampleapp: x-request-id lost in background tasks (setImmediate/worker_threads); ALS reinjection + redaction semantics" (assigned devex).

jo: thanks — I'll link PR and add the small repro to quickstart docs as a note until fix lands.
